Corrosion control and interpretation of tests — NPL (@mat-npl-degradation: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_6SEQ1G67MES2K0JB6X7AEA4WD6
[Corrosion Control for Pumps and Valves](https://eprintspublications.npl.co.uk/8618/), R. Francis, edited by A. Turnbull and G. Hinds, 2020; [28-page guide](https://eprintspublications.npl.co.uk/8618/1/Corrosion%20Guide%20No%206.pdf). Read the full guide for environment, construction material, flow, localized attack, damage under stress and practical control.

Then read A. Turnbull, *Stress corrosion cracking of duplex stainless steels in concentrated brines—a critique of testing*, NPL DEPC-MPE 008, 2005: [publication](https://eprintspublications.npl.co.uk/3156/), [27-page report](https://eprintspublications.npl.co.uk/3156/1/DEPC_MPE8.pdf). Compare ranking tests with qualification for actual service; follow temperature, wetting, salt chemistry, oxygen and specimen geometry.

Contents and selected mechanism, drop-evaporation and test-interpretation passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. Historical methods do not establish current standard requirements. The guide requires permission for copying and the report carries Crown copyright. These are free external readings, not openly licensed text to redistribute.

**Return:** [Materials-engineering sources — reading and primary evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_51JAH6DB4WV2HZAB69G21ZHSMK).
